<<<<<<< SEARCH
    if (nights < LONG_STAY) return full;
    // the discount is rounded down, in the yard's favour
    return full - Math.floor((full * LONG_STAY_OFF) / 100);
=======
    // the first LONG_STAY nights are charged in full
    if (nights <= LONG_STAY) return full;
    // the discount applies only to the nights after the first week,
    // worked out once on their total and rounded down, in the yard's favour
    const later = (nights - LONG_STAY) * rate;
    return full - Math.floor((later * LONG_STAY_OFF) / 100);
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

I changed `stayFee` so the discount is calculated only on the total for nights after the seventh, using the same 10% rate and the same round-down. Stays of seven nights or fewer now get no discount, and I reused `LONG_STAY` (7) as the number of full-price nights.

I couldn't open or run anything, so this is untested. I also couldn't see whether other code relies on `LONG_STAY` meaning "discount starts at 7 nights".
